      "content": "That seems like a pretty extreme stance to take. You're basically saying it's more important to have a random chance than to actually help the people in the most crisis. If a policy doesn't prioritize the most vulnerable, how is that 'equitable' in any meaningful sense? Aren't you just ignoring the whole point of social welfare programs by pushing for a lottery?",
